# Go tooling writes LF and expects it back. Without this, a checkout on
# Windows converts Go sources to CRLF and gofmt reports every file as
# unformatted, so `gofmt -l` and any check built on it are useless there.
#
# The generated tables are the same: their generators write LF, and a
# CRLF working copy makes every regeneration look like a rewrite.
*.go text eol=lf

# The data the generators read, and the scripts that produce it.
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Task definitions and documentation.
justfile text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# The committed diagrams are generated by the pvdiagram example, so they
# fall under the same rule as the tables above: the generator writes LF,
# and a CRLF working copy makes every regeneration look like a rewrite.
*.svg text eol=lf

# Extracted book pages and raster images are binary.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
